==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*per-|id1=before|*men-|id2=stand out}}
From obsolete {{der|en|fr|prominent}} (compare {{m|fr|proéminent}}), from {{der|en|la|prōminēns}}, present active participle of {{m|la|prōmineō|t=jut out, to project}}, from {{m|la|prō|t=before, forward}} + {{m|la||mineō}} (in compounds, “[[jut]], [[project]]”).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpɹɑmɪnənt/|a=GA}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpɹɒmɪnənt/|a=RP}}
* {{hyph|en|prom|i|nent}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-prominent.ogg|a=US}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Standing out, or [[project]]ing; jutting; [[protuberant]].
#: {{syn|en|extuberant|outstanding|Thesaurus:protuberant}}
#: {{ant|en|improminent}}
#: {{ux|en|The bird was perching on the '''prominent''' ledge at the top of the rocks}}
# Likely to attract attention from its size or position; [[conspicuous]].
#: {{syn|en|attention-grabbing|eye-catching|flashy|Thesaurus:conspicuous}}
#: {{ant|en|improminent|Thesaurus:inconspicuous}}
#: {{ux|en|Place the slogan in a more '''prominent''' position.}}
# [[eminent|Eminent]]; distinguished above others.
#: {{syn|en|eminent|forestanding|noteworthy|Thesaurus:notable}}
#: {{ant|en|improminent|Thesaurus:normal}}
#: {{ux|en|'''prominent''' members of the press}}

